<http://www.spektrix.com/kelownacommunitytheatre/event/404601ABDRHBJKVGJGBDQJVHKNJCBRCJC>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "Ballet Kelowna - Double Take";
  schema:description """
	<table class=\" BorderOn\">
		<tr>
			<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"1\"><img src=\"https://system.spektrix.com/kelownacommunitytheatre/files/e2c839aa-8091-4a6a-8a5e-6b5ea6935a9d.jpg\" /> </td><td align=\"left\"><h2>Ballet Kelowna presents </h2><h1><span class=\"UnderlineText\">DOUBLE TAKE</span></h1><h2><span class=\"BoldText\">May 14 + 15, 2027</span></h2><span class=\"BoldText\">Friday at 7:30 PM / Saturday at 1:30 PM and 7:30 PM</span></td>
		</tr>
	</table><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><h2><span class=\"BoldText\"><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.theboxoffice.ca/ballet-kelowna-202627\">2026/27 subscriptions on sale now.</a></span></h2><h2>Single tickets on sale September 14, 2026.</h2><span><br/></span> ---<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><h2>A double bill celebrating Kurt Werner’s outstanding career with Ballet Kelowna</h2><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">WORLD PREMIERE</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">New Work by Alyssa Martin</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Choreography:</span> Alyssa Martin <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Ontario-based choreographer Alyssa Martin draws inspiration from Harold Lander’s 1948 ballet <span class=\"ItalicText\">Études</span> in a lively new creation that reimagines classical technique. With a distinctive background in contemporary dance, musical theatre, and absurdism, Martin cleverly dismantles conventions to reveal the individuality of each performer. Blending humour, vulnerability, and virtuosic movement, this joyful new work embodies authenticity, connection, and the evolving language of ballet.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>“[Martin’s] choreography is athletic and precise, with sharp, angular gestures balanced by fluid, expansive movements that explore the body’s full potential.” - <span class=\"ItalicText\">The Dance Debrief</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Mustard</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Choreography:</span> Robert Stephen<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Composer:</span> Owen Belton<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>An imaginary friend refuses to fade away in Robert Stephen's playful and witty <span class=\"ItalicText\">Mustard</span>. Adapted from Kat Sandler's Dora Mavor Moore Award-winning play, this charming ballet follows an endearing imaginary friend whose unexpected adventures blur the line between fantasy and reality. Returning to the role he originated for the work's 2024 world premiere, Kurt Werner brings warmth, humour, and heart to the title character in his final performances with Ballet Kelowna. Paired with Owen Belton's vibrant original score, <span class=\"ItalicText\">Mustard</span> offers audiences a whimsical celebration of imagination and a memorable final showcase for one of Ballet Kelowna's beloved artists.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Ballet Kelowna’s 2026/27 season is presented by the Thomas Alan Budd Foundation<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>---<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Subscriptions on sale until November 7, 2026. Single tickets on sale September 14, 2026. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">A service fee is added for box office costs, card processing, and taxes. <span class=\"BoldText\">Ballet Kelowna</span> tickets and their applicable fees are non-refundable.</span>
""";
  schema:startDate "2027-05-14T19:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
