g to the role he originated for the work's 2024 world premiere, Kurt Werner brings warmth, humour, and heart to the title character in his final performances with Ballet Kelowna. Paired with Owen Belton's vibrant original score, <span class=\"ItalicText\">Mustard</span> offers audiences a whimsical celebration of imagination and a memorable final showcase for one of Ballet Kelowna's beloved artists.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Ballet Kelowna’s 2026/27 season is presented by the Thomas Alan Budd Foundation<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>---<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Subscriptions on sale until November 7, 2026. Single tickets on sale September 14, 2026. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">A service fee is added for box office costs, card processing, and taxes. <span class=\"BoldText\">Ballet Kelowna</span> tickets and their applicable fees are non-refundable.</span>
