<http://www.spektrix.com/kelownacommunitytheatre/event/404001ABLSVNGCNGHCSNHBGTVTPDKDMGK>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "Ballet Kelowna - Four Voices";
  schema:description """
	<table class=\" BorderOn\">
		<tr>
			<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"1\"><img src=\"https://system.spektrix.com/kelownacommunitytheatre/files/af5f71f8-1821-49bb-ab1b-b0d10c16bc78.jpg\" /> </td><td align=\"left\"><h2>Ballet Kelowna presents </h2><h1><span class=\"UnderlineText\">FOUR VOICES</span></h1><h2><span class=\"BoldText\">November 6 + 7, 2026</span></h2><span class=\"BoldText\">Friday at 7:30 PM / Saturday at 1:30 PM and 7:30 PM</span></td>
		</tr>
	</table><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><h2><span class=\"BoldText\"><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.theboxoffice.ca/ballet-kelowna-202627\">2026/27 subscriptions on sale now.</a></span></h2><h2>Single tickets on sale September 14, 2026.</h2><span><br/></span> ---<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><h2>A curated mixed program bringing together four choreographic visions</h2><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">WORLD PREMIERE</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">New Work by Joanna Lige</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Choreography:</span> Joanna Lige<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Joanna Lige returns with a striking new work inspired by the resilience of the natural world. In the face of environmental destruction, beauty may appear fragile, yet beneath the surface lies an extraordinary capacity to survive. Through richly expressive movement, Lige explores the grief of ecological loss while affirming nature's quiet persistence.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Acts of Remembrance</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Choreography:</span> Simone Orlando<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Composer:</span> Owen Belton <span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">Acts of Remembrance</span> is a poignant tribute to those who served and gave their lives in times of war. Set to the sweeping, emotive score of Canadian composer Owen Belton, the work reflects on the profound human cost of conflict, drawing inspiration from pivotal First World War battles including Vimy Ridge and Passchendaele. Combining arresting imagery with stirring music, <span class=\"ItalicText\">Acts of Remembrance</span> honours the courage, sacrifice, and enduring legacy of the Canadians who faced these defining moments in history.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">WORLD PREMIERE</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">New Work by Donaldo Nava</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Choreography:</span> Donaldo Nava<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Company dancer Donaldo Nava makes his solo choreographic debut with a heartfelt new work created for Kurt Werner, who concludes his final season with Ballet Kelowna. With intimate solos and a vivid duet, the piece contemplates the relationships that shape us and the lasting bonds forged through dance.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">The Reassuring Effects (of Form and Poetry)</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Choreography:</span> Trey McIntyre<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Back by popular demand, Trey McIntyre's <span class=\"ItalicText\">The Reassuring Effects (of Form and Poetry)</span> delights with its infectious energy, musicality, and spirit. Set to Antonín Dvořák's radiant <span class=\"ItalicText\">Serenade for Strings in E Major</span>, this exhilarating work showcases eight dancers in a dazzling display of speed, precision, and uplifting movement that the <span class=\"ItalicText\">Miami Herald</span> described as moving \"with the speed and clarity of light.\"<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Ballet Kelowna’s 2026/27 season is presented by the Thomas Alan Budd Foundation<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>---<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Subscriptions on sale until November 7, 2026. Single tickets on sale September 14, 2026.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">A service fee is added for box office costs, card processing, and taxes. <span class=\"BoldText\">Ballet Kelowna</span> tickets and their applicable fees are non-refundable.</span>
""";
  schema:startDate "2026-11-06T19:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
  schema:image <https://system.spektrix.com/kelownacommunitytheatre/files/af5f71f8-1821-49bb-ab1b-b0d10c16bc78.jpg>;
