<http://www.spektrix.com/kelownacommunitytheatre/event/410001AGLCQVPCQBVPHRTKRRMPBRGRRSQ>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "New World Men";
  schema:description """
	<table class=\" BorderOn\">
		<tr>
			<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"1\"><img src=\"https://system.spektrix.com/kelownacommunitytheatre/files/686f1013-5a11-46e4-8845-b1b98f354446.jpg\" /> </td><td align=\"left\"><h2>New World Men present </h2><h1><span class=\"UnderlineText\">NEW WORLD MEN</span></h1><h2><span class=\"ItalicText\"><span class=\"BoldText\">The Sound of RUSH</span></span></h2></td>
		</tr>
	</table><span><br/></span>New World Men's goal is to reproduce the sound of the legendary Canadian band RUSH, on stage.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>New World Men was formed in the summer of 2014 and has since performed hundreds of shows — many of them sold out — earning a reputation as Canada's most technically precise and musically authentic RUSH tribute act.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>The project took shape in the winter of 2014 when Marc Girard, encouraged by the renowned Martin Levac — widely regarded as one of the world's leading Phil Collins interpreters — set out to build a RUSH tribute rooted in uncompromising musicianship. He joined forces with guitarist Frank Larouche, and together they committed to faithfully recreating the RUSH live experience in every detail.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>The lineup was completed with the addition of Matt Grou, whose extraordinary ability to simultaneously handle Neil Peart's demanding drum parts and Geddy Lee's soaring vocal lines became the cornerstone of the band's identity. With three musicians of this calibre on stage, New World Men doesn't just play RUSH — they inhabit it.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>---<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><h2>Pricing</h2><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Regular  $59.00</span>  ($48.94 base price + $2.36 CIF + $7.70 service charge)<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">All above prices include GST.</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span>---<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">Mary Irwin Theatre event tickets include a $2.36 Capital Improvement Fee (CIF). A service fee is added for box office costs, card processing, and taxes. <span class=\"BoldText\">New World Men</span> tickets and their applicable fees are non-refundable.</span>
""";
