  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "The Dinner Theatre";
  schema:description """
	<table class=\" BorderOn\">
		<tr>
			<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"1\"><img src=\"https://system.spektrix.com/kelownacommunitytheatre/files/d86af45a-4e9f-4930-958b-ec1f59bd580d.jpg\" /> </td><td align=\"left\"><h2>The Creative House presents </h2><h1><span class=\"UnderlineText\">THE DINNER THEATRE</span></h1><h2><span class=\"ItalicText\"><span class=\"BoldText\">in association with Geek SOS Services Ltd.</span></span></h2></td>
		</tr>
	</table><span><br/></span>Two Broadway legends. One dinner theatre in Moncton New Brunswick. A show that was never supposed to matter — until it did. When faded leading man Liam Mitchell finds himself starring opposite the woman he let go twenty-five years ago, an emergency cast replacement turns into an unexpected reckoning. Confined to a cramped dressing room between scenes of <span class=\"ItalicText\">Fiddler on the Roof</span>, with a stage manager who has a plan for everything (including, apparently, love), old wounds reopen backstage — and a story meant to unfold behind the curtain becomes bigger than the show itself. Featuring a soaring original score of ballads and showstoppers, <span class=\"ItalicText\">The Dinner Theatre</span> is a bittersweet, funny, and deeply human story about second acts — on stage and off.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Written by Canadian recording artist <span class=\"BoldText\">Rick Worrall</span>, who also stars as Liam Mitchell, this world premiere production will be produced by The Creative House, directed by <span class=\"BoldText\">Angela Quinn</span> with music direction by <span class=\"BoldText\">Neville Bowman</span>. Kelowna favourite <span class=\"BoldText\">Gwen Plitt</span> returns to the stage as Sarah Rogers, with soprano supreme <span class=\"BoldText\">Carmen Harris</span> as the whirlwind stage manager Cheryl holding it all together. Don't miss the world premiere of a musical about the moments that happen when the applause fades and the mirror doesn't lie.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>PLEASE NOTE: The Dinner Theatre is the title of the musical. There is no dinner service included with this event.  <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>---<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><h2>Pricing</h2><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Regular  $44.00</span>  ($40.00 base price + $4.00 service charge)<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">All above prices are in CAD and include GST.</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span>---<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">A service fee is added for box office costs, card processing, and taxes. Tickets for <span class=\"BoldText\">The Dinner Theatre</span> and their applicable service fees are non-refundable.</span>
""";
