<http://www.spektrix.com/kelownacommunitytheatre/event/387001ASGVHBBDVPLPDDSHPNNRRQCNRKH>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "Train Wreck Comedy Concert Series - Dino Archie's K-Town Comedy Extravaganza";
  schema:description """
	<table class=\" BorderOn\">
		<tr>
			<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"1\"><img src=\"https://system.spektrix.com/kelownacommunitytheatre/files/0ca92dc0-ebd2-4af8-9ad4-6aca7f529551.jpg\" /> </td><td align=\"left\"><h2>Train Wreck Comedy Concert Series presents </h2><h1><span class=\"UnderlineText\">DINO ARCHIE'S K-TOWN COMEDY EXTRAVAGANZA</span></h1><h2>presented by Freddy's Brewpub</h2></td>
		</tr>
	</table><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Dino Archie</span> - Originally from Fresno, California, Dino Archie is one of stand-up comedy’s most naturally funny and charismatic performers. Now based in Vancouver, Dino has appeared on Comedy Central’s <span class=\"ItalicText\">Adam Devine’s House Party</span> and <span class=\"ItalicText\">Jimmy Kimmel Live!</span>, while earning recognition as a Just For Laughs New Face, Seattle International Comedy Competition winner, and Best Crowd Work winner at Just For Laughs Northwest and Kevin Hart’s LOL Network. His credits also include NPR’s <span class=\"ItalicText\">Snap Judgment</span>, <span class=\"ItalicText\">Don’t Tell Comedy</span>, Crave’s Russell Peters Gala, CBC Gem Originals, and Amazon Prime’s <span class=\"ItalicText\">Inside Jokes</span>. With laid-back confidence and razor-sharp crowd work, Dino makes every show feel unforgettable. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Brett Forte</span> - Brett Forte is one of Canada’s fastest-rising comedy exports, earning titles like Yuk Yuk’s Top New Comic and Edmonton’s Funniest Person before being selected as a Just For Laughs New Face in 2019. A favorite at the Hollywood Comedy Festival, Brett has appeared on <span class=\"ItalicText\">The Fighter and The Kid</span>, <span class=\"ItalicText\">Joke WRLD</span>, and <span class=\"ItalicText\">The Uncle Lazer Podcas</span>t. After nearly a decade headlining across Canada, Brett now lives in Austin, Texas — supposedly for comedy, though there may also be a warrant involved. Known for fearless storytelling and unpredictable energy, Brett now headlines clubs across the U.S. including The Hollywood Improv, Phoenix House of Comedy, and Hyena’s Comedy Clubs. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Yumi Nagashima</span> - is a Tokyo-born actress, writer, and international stand-up comedian known for her magnetic stage presence and sharp, globally informed perspective. Blending cultural insight with playful elegance and bold timing, she captivates audiences worldwide. Her work has been featured at Just For Laughs Montreal, Winnipeg Comedy Festival, Halifax Comedy Festival, CBC Gem’s New Wave of Stand-Up, and Comedy Central Asia. Her viral comedy clips across social media and YouTube continue to reach a rapidly growing global audience. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>---<span><br/></span><h2>Pricing</h2><span class=\"BoldText\">Regular  $65.00</span>  ($54.16 base price + $2.36 CIF + $8.48 service charge)<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">All above prices are CAD and include GST.</span><span><br/></span>---<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">The Train Wreck Comedy Concert Series is bringing five unforgettable nights of world-class stand-up comedy to the Rotary Centre for the Arts, featuring some of the funniest professional comedians from across North America. <span class=\"BoldText\">Freddy’s Brewpub is proud to be the Official Beer Sponsor</span> of the series, serving great local craft beer at all five performances while audiences enjoy razor-sharp storytelling, side-splitting crowd work, huge energy, big personalities, and nonstop laughs.  Whether you're a die-hard comedy fan or just looking for an incredible night out, this is the must-see comedy event series of the year!</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.theboxoffice.ca/season-tickets/train-wreck-comedy-concert-series\">Purchase a Series Package Here!</a><span><br/></span><span><br/></span>---<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">Mary Irwin Theatre at the Rotary Centre for the Arts event tickets include a $2.36 Capital Improvement Fee (CIF). A service fee is added for box office costs, card processing, and taxes. <span class=\"BoldText\">Dino Archie's Extravaganza</span> tickets and their applicable fees are non-refundable.</span>
""";
