<http://www.spektrix.com/kelownacommunitytheatre/event/411001AKTDKVPHNTBRBRLSNQJTRHPCPVG>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "UBC Okanagan Debates: Are We Failing Youth?";
  schema:description """
	<table class=\" BorderOn\">
		<tr>
			<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"1\"><img src=\"https://system.spektrix.com/kelownacommunitytheatre/files/26664492-35b2-47db-8d22-ec17b4d1e19b.jpg\" /> </td><td align=\"left\"><h2>UBC Okanagan presents </h2><h1><span class=\"UnderlineText\">UBC OKANAGAN DEBATES</span></h1><h2><span class=\"ItalicText\"><span class=\"BoldText\">Are We Failing Youth?</span></span></h2></td>
		</tr>
	</table><span><br/></span>Few questions divide Canadians, and generations, more sharply. Young adults face housing they can't afford, entry-level work reshaped by AI, and a mental-health crisis their parents never named. Yet they are also the best-educated, healthiest and most connected generation in history, holding tools no one before them had. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Both sides agree on the facts. They disagree strongly on what they add up to. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>On September 16, four distinguished voices will tackle the question: <span class=\"BoldText\">Are we leaving a better world for the next generation?</span> Two will argue yes. Two will argue no. You decide. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>---<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">This is a free event with assigned seating. Tickets can be booked online through our Box Office.</span>
""";
